W3-0a part 4 (applyBudget: trim lists of over-budget results; skip an over-budget first row of a page)
Base commit: 7a9fcc0ecc40e7e851bce06ce59cc8f65d8113fa
Status: parked until the breadth gate after 3 reviewer FAILs.
Contents: src/ops/registry.ts, test/format.test.ts (budget tests), src/sched/scheduler.ts (resultBudget comment),
and the RX-1/budget-trim row of docs/ledger/parity/reax.jsonl, as a diff against the base commit.
Apply from the repository root with: git apply <this file>

Reviewer round-3 finding (open):
  the skip note (registry.ts:158) and the page-shortened note (registry.ts:91-96) are added after trimInto and
  never counted, so data plus notes can exceed the 1 MiB budget; reproduced (2 MiB row + 150,000-string list
  gives 1,048,673 bytes; page-shortened 1,048,656); reviewer fuzz 2,472 of 20,000 cases over;
  format.test.ts:579 allows the overshoot.

Reviewer's proposed fix:
  reserve room for the skip note in the last trimLists call; in the lo>0 branch size the prefix against data
  plus shortNote, binary search included; tighten line 579 to <= 1000; add a 1 MiB test that fails on
  today's code.

Open ruling (for the user):
  trimInto counts notes and so raises result_too_large on results that would fit with every list emptied
  (248 of 20,000); this contradicts the trimLists comment at registry.ts:262.

Line numbers refer to the files as this patch leaves them.

